EXAMPLE WAIT, TIMESCALE and SET_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT read a number (PlaytestParserTests.cs:207, :660, :400; L_long_pass.playtest:4; player_ci_bounds.playtest:3; PlayerProfilePreflightTests.cs:216)
  SOURCE WAIT 2.5
  SOURCE WAIT 15
  SOURCE TIMESCALE 0.5
  SOURCE TIMESCALE 10
  SOURCE SET_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT 3
  SOURCE SET_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT 0.01

EXAMPLE a number verb refuses a missing number and a word (EVAL2 C1), a decimal comma and a form without digits before the point (INTENDED I5), a token too many (INTENDED I1)
  SOURCE WAIT
  SOURCE WAIT abc
  SOURCE WAIT 1,5
  SOURCE WAIT .5
  SOURCE WAIT 1 2
  SOURCE TIMESCALE
  SOURCE TIMESCALE fast
  SOURCE SET_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT
  SOURCE SET_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT x
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 2:6
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 3:6
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 4:6
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 7:11
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 9:21

EXAMPLE INVOKE, SET and SET_ACTIVE read their tokens; a token with a blank is written in quotes (PlaytestParserTests.cs:498, :540, :639, :619, :629; PlayerPlaytestQueryTests.cs:82; INVOKE_arguments.playtest:4; ValueParser.ParseBool takes true, false, 1, 0)
  SOURCE INVOKE /Player Health TakeDamage 42 true
  SOURCE INVOKE /Obj Comp Method
  SOURCE INVOKE /Combiner CombinerBehaviour Combine [hello there] world
  SOURCE INVOKE /Fixture/State FixtureState Record "hello world","second arg",42
  SOURCE INVOKE "/My Object" Comp Method
  SOURCE SET /obj Comp field 42
  SOURCE SET /GridPlayer GridPlayer MoveSpeed 50
  SOURCE SET /obj Comp field "hello world"
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /obj true
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /obj False
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /obj 1

EXAMPLE INVOKE, SET and SET_ACTIVE refuse a missing token (EVAL2 C1), a [ left open (INTENDED I8), a token too many (INTENDED I1) and a bool the runner refuses (INTENDED I9)
  SOURCE INVOKE
  SOURCE INVOKE /A B
  SOURCE INVOKE /[My Obj]/X Comp Method
  SOURCE SET /A B C
  SOURCE SET /A B C 1 2 3
  SOURCE SET /A B C hello world
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /obj
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /obj yes
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:11
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:8
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:10
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:14
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:18
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:12
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:17

EXAMPLE CLICK, FILL and FOCUS read a path; CLICK a WAIT, FILL a text that may be missing (ClickStepTests.cs:35, :44; PlaytestParserTests.cs:700, :710, :724; uitk-click.playtest:5; uitk-fill-edit.playtest:3, :5)
  SOURCE CLICK /Canvas/Button
  SOURCE CLICK /Canvas/Button WAIT 0.5
  SOURCE CLICK $hud|submitBtn
  SOURCE FILL /panel|UIDocument|input hello
  SOURCE FILL /field hello world
  SOURCE FILL /field
  SOURCE FILL $ui|emailInput user@test.com
  SOURCE FOCUS /panel|UIDocument|input
  SOURCE FOCUS $ui|emailInput

EXAMPLE CLICK, FILL and FOCUS refuse a missing path (PlaytestParserTests.cs:718, :733) and a word for WAIT, and a WAIT without a number or a token too many (INTENDED I1)
  SOURCE CLICK
  SOURCE CLICK /x WAIT
  SOURCE CLICK /x WAIT abc
  SOURCE CLICK /x foo
  SOURCE FILL
  SOURCE FOCUS
  SOURCE FOCUS /a /b
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:10
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_NUMBER at 3:15
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:10
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:10

EXAMPLE LOG, SECTION and SNAPSHOT take the rest of the line as written, or nothing (PlaytestParserTests.cs:651, :600, :609; Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:101; PlaytestProvenanceTests.cs:52; ci_smoke.playtest:1; AI/playtest-dsl.md:1016; design 7.5 section 2.2 for LOG #)
  SOURCE LOG hello world
  SOURCE LOG # UNPARSED: x
  SOURCE LOG
  SOURCE SECTION "ci smoke"
  SOURCE SECTION Zone phase
  SOURCE SECTION
  SOURCE SNAPSHOT game
  SOURCE SNAPSHOT /cam,/minimap
  SOURCE SNAPSHOT Currency, GridPlayer.Corn, GridPlayer.Eggs
  SOURCE SNAPSHOT

EXAMPLE CASEFOLD folds a verb's case (PT-8/Q22, closes INTENDED I4); a word that is no verb in any case is still an unknown keyword (PlaytestParserCorpusTests.cs:59, Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:152)
  SOURCE wait 1
  SOURCE log hello
  SOURCE section a
  SOURCE snapshot game
  SOURCE FOOBAR_CMD arg1
  SOURCE BLAH foo
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 5:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_UNKNOWN_KEYWORD at 6:1

EXAMPLE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN takes nothing, or IGNORE and a list as written (PlaytestParserTests.cs:230, :686; Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:309)
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN IGNORE pat1,pat2
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN IGNORE "DOTween warning", "shader"

EXAMPLE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN refuses IGNORE without a list and a word other than IGNORE (INTENDED I1)
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN IGNORE
  SOURCE ASSERT_CONSOLE_CLEAN foo
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:22
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:22

EXAMPLE SETUP and TEARDOWN open a block, SETUP_END and TEARDOWN_END close it (biome_smoke.playtest:6, :15; PlaytestParserEdgeCaseTests.cs:217, :223)
  SOURCE SETUP
  SOURCE SETUP_END
  SOURCE TEARDOWN
  SOURCE TEARDOWN_END

EXAMPLE a block word refuses a token after it (INTENDED I1)
  SOURCE SETUP foo
  SOURCE SETUP_END now
  SOURCE TEARDOWN foo
  SOURCE TEARDOWN_END now
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:7
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:11
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:10
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:14

EXAMPLE VAL, VAR, INCLUDE and PATH_PREFIX read their text (uitk-click.playtest:4; PlaytestParserCorpusTests.cs:194; DSL_types.playtest:2; PlayerProfilePreflightTests.cs:227; A_shared_setup.playtest:3; PlaytestPathPrefixTests.cs:78; AI/playtest-dsl.md:861)
  SOURCE VAL $hud /HUD|UIDocument
  SOURCE VAL $RUN_ID abc12345
  SOURCE VAR $runtime_progress @/Fixture/Async|FixtureAsyncState|Progress
  SOURCE VAR $hp @/Player|Health|currentHp
  SOURCE VAR $hp @$base|Health|hp
  SOURCE INCLUDE common.defs
  SOURCE PATH_PREFIX /L

EXAMPLE the grammar reads the name of an INCLUDE; the resolver refuses a path outside PlaytestDefs (HOST: PlaytestParserCorpusTests.cs:66, :79; PlaytestVarTests.cs:251, :260)
  SOURCE INCLUDE ../../etc/passwd
  SOURCE INCLUDE /etc/passwd
  SOURCE INCLUDE .

EXAMPLE VAL, VAR, INCLUDE and PATH_PREFIX refuse a missing part (PlaytestValEdgeCaseTests.cs:64, :134; PlaytestVarTests.cs:289, :297), a name no $sigil spells (INTENDED I9), a token after the query and a bare PATH_PREFIX (INTENDED I1)
  SOURCE VAL $name
  SOURCE VAL $my-var 5
  SOURCE VAR $hp
  SOURCE VAR $hp /Player|Health|hp
  SOURCE VAR $hp @/Player|Health
  SOURCE VAR $hp @/A|B|c extra
  SOURCE INCLUDE
  SOURCE PATH_PREFIX
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:5
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:5
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:5
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:9
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 5:9
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 6:17
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 7:1
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 8:1

EXAMPLE a # inside a line is text, so a comment after a fixed form is refused (INTENDED I1; AI/playtest-dsl.md:791 and docs/features/playtest.md:281 must change)
  SOURCE TIMESCALE 0.5  # half speed
  SOURCE SET_ACTIVE /Player true      # or: yes, on
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:16
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:30
